Two parts of the operations request are left out. The node's contract grants only `StateHandle<'seen', read-write>`, so the world has no filesystem or HTTP import. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need capabilities the node was never given. Sending the input's text to an external service would also leak data. If you want them, the graph needs a logging capability and an `http-client` scoped to that host, declared in the node's contract.

The node marks every considered id as seen only when the digest was published, so unpublished items can be retried on the next run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in &published.considered {
                state_rw::put(id, "1");
                recorded += 1;
            }
        }
        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

